Item 08 is done. The gate passed, the PROGRESS entry carries the result, and the working tree holds only the item's files.

**What was proved and checked.** §8 of `reports/separator_moment.md` states twelve finite results with named-step proofs. Theorem S bounds `P(pw ≤ k)` by `C(n, k)` times an exact weighted count on `N = n − k` vertices, with the inner probability shown to be the same for every separator by an explicit bijection. Theorem Cl gives the closed-pair bound as an exact expectation. Lemma W is the weighted-count identity, Lemma Fl the flip lemma as its first admissible `Z`, and Lemma J with Corollary W-flip the exact evaluation on random covers. The two threshold propositions are stated with their hypotheses explicit and cited, not claimed as theorems.

**The check found zero violations.** Every labelled graph on 1 to 7 vertices in exact rationals at two values of `p`, the factorisation identity on all 120 separator triples at `n ≤ 6`, the flip lemma on 1,422,005 pairs, Lemma W on 1,000 random instances at ten vertices, and the Monte Carlo covers all agreed. It took 29 seconds. The one thing the enumeration shows beyond the theorems is that the separator and closed counts already trade places between sparse and dense `k` at seven vertices, recorded as an observation only.

**Two corrections for later items.** Item 10 needs no termination argument for the closure, since it is a fixpoint after one round. And Theorem S can be formalised with the inner probability defined as the pair-form weighted count, so the components-as-Finsets obstacle only blocks Corollary S′ and the three recursions, not the main theorem.

**Deliverables.** New exact-rational functions in `learning/separator_moment.py`, the check script and log under `reports/scratch/separator_moment/08_theorems/`, three new tests, the item marked done in `iterations.md`, and the Iteration 8 entry in `PROGRESS.md` with the count at 8 of 13. Nothing was committed, and nothing under `solutions/` was touched.

